    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Tivoli sits 30 kilometres northeast of Rome, where the Aniene River spills into the Sabine Hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli%2C_Lazio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s ancient name, Tibur, may share a root with the river Tiber and the Latin praenomen Tiberius.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli%2C_Lazio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Legend says Tibur was founded by Catillus, an Arcadian son of Amphiaraus, who fled Thebes after a massacre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli%2C_Lazio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tivoli’s Roman heritage includes the ruins of Hadrian’s Villa, a UNESCO World Heritage site built in the early second century AD.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli%2C_Lazio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s historic centre still shows defensive walls from the Roman era, built in opus quadratum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tivoli%2C_Lazio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Tivoli is celebrated for its natural beauty, with the Aniene Falls and the nearby Villa d’Este adding to its cultural landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
